sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Acetabularia acetabulum Turing wavelength at 25.28 µm (Holocene, detail scale) — MorphoEval overall 89.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2. Same Brusselator and tier length (25.28 µm, 2.528e-5 m, 0 Ma). Inhibitor D_axial/D_hoop swept over {0.35, 0.45, 0.70, 1.00, 1.60}: hoop mode wins at 0.45 (|mode| 8 vs 1) and the axial mode wins at 1.60 (|mode| 8 vs 1). Seeded grain drops rendered coherency from 0.87 to 0.54, beside the CC0 cap at 0.62. GIF CV similarity 87.3 (12 frames, 640x480). Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9996, wavelength-sweep Pearson r = 0.99999, RMSE 0.23 µm. Ablation ratio 0.097. Orientation KS = 0.191. Saturated peak 25.08 µm versus tier 25.28 µm. Overall 89.9/100 (faithfulness 89.8, reproducibility 90.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit bd2c74bc; environment: python 3.12.3, note Pass 2 on the same VM. Nanopub profile absent, so the KG is unsigned.. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/acetabularia_acetabulum_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0.py at bd2c74bc, image/gif, 4027264 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 48f30bdef7c6420215c169bc392f46857a15535c9cf793a90b0b70b33c03e8c9 (sha256 48f30bdef7c6420215c169bc392f46857a15535c9cf793a90b0b70b33c03e8c9), spec_fingerprint 96087cd4e2bc623a26b35d593a33788c367131953ba2d7b731f791fb3ce2cc1b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 96087cd4e2bc623a26b35d593a33788c367131953ba2d7b731f791fb3ce2cc1b; artifact_sha256: 48f30bdef7c6420215c169bc392f46857a15535c9cf793a90b0b70b33c03e8c9; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/acetabularia_acetabulum_turing_wavelength_s0/acetabularia_acetabulum_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=3e562916ba2ad34f..., datasets/acetabularia_acetabulum_turing_wavelength_s0/acetabularia_acetabulum_wikimedia_cc0.jpg=0773237a26517128...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber. | Dumais & Harrison 2000: reaction-diffusion is the favoured whorl mechanism in Acetabularia. | Holloway & Harrison 2007: Brusselator kinetics on a plant surface can make whorls.; reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivities placing the fastest mode at 25.43 µm, next to the 25.28 µm tier length. | Axial/hoop sweep showing the ridge axis flips as the ratio crosses 1. | Seeded grain on the face-on cap, not a copy of the photograph.; transfer_boundary: 25.28 µm is the slot's tier length. The papers discuss whorl spacing without publishing this number. | The model disk (radius 354 µm) is the geometry implied by 88 ridges at that wavelength, not a traced outline of the adult CC0 cap.; does_not_claim: Pixel identity with the CC0 photograph or the gallery plate. | A measured value for the axial/hoop diffusivity ratio. | A second chronospecies, or any reuse of sibling slot 192's template constants.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=1.1]: Independent second assessor has not reviewed the pass-2 scores.",
            "remediation needed: A second assessor from another provider has not scored these dimensions.",
            "remediation needed: The 354 µm model cap is not a landmark registration of the adult CC0 photograph.",
            "remediation needed: The axial/hoop ratio is bounded by the sweep but was not measured on a cell." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.899"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

